                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
                with connection;
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
                with connection.
          %p
            The study of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
          %p
            The next higher degree analog of the electromagnetic field is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
          %h2#mathematical_model_from_formal_physical_input Mathematical model from (formal) physical input
          %p
            The derivation of the fact that the Kalb-Ramond field that is locally given by a 2-form is globally really a degree 3 cocycle in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            proceeds in in entire analogy with the corresponding discussion of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong classical background
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
                3-form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \in \Omega^3(X)
                is required to be closed,
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mn 3
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d H_3 = 0
            %li
              %p
                %strong quantum coupling
                The gauge interaction with the quantum string is required to yield a well-defined surface holonomy in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                from locally integrating the 2-forms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_i \in \Omega^2(U_2)
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi H
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d B_i = H|_{U_i}
                over its 2-dimensional trajectory.
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hol
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mi f
                        %mi exp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mi f
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo *
                          %msub
                            %mi B
                            %mrow
                              %mi ρ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %msub
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                              %mrow
                                %mi e
                                %mo ⊂
                                %mi f
                            %mi exp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                              %msub
                                %mo ∫
                                %mi e
                              %msup
                                %mi Σ
                                %mo *
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi e
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi v
                                    %mo ⊂
                                    %mi e
                                    %mo ⊂
                                    %mi f
                                %mi exp
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %msub
                                  %mi λ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi ρ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mi ρ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi e
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mi ρ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi v
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      hol(\Sigma)
                      \=
                      \\textstyle{\prod}_{f}
                      \\exp(i \textstyle{\int}_f \Sigma^* B_{\rho(f)})
                      \\textstyle{\prod}_{e \subset f}
                      \\exp(i \textstyle{\int}_{e} \Sigma^* A_{\rho(f) \rho(e)})
                      \\textstyle{\prod}_{v \subset e \subset f}
                      \\exp(i \lambda_{\rho(f) \rho(e) \rho(v)})
                      \\,.
              %p That this is well defined requires that
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi l
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                          %mi l
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                          %mi l
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi mod
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mn 2
                      %mi π
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\lambda_{i j k} - \lambda_{i j l} +
                      \\lambda_{i k l} - \lambda_{j k l}
                      \= 0 \;mod \, 2\pi
                      \\,,
              %p
                which says that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B_i, A_{i j}, \lambda_{i j k})
                is indeed a degree 3
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cocycle
          %h2#over_dbranes Over D-branes
          %p
            The restriction of the Kalb-Ramond field in the 10-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            is a twist (as in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            on the D-brane: its 3-class is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+charge"} magnetic charge
            for the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+field"} Yang-Mills field
            on the D-brane. See also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten+anomaly+cancellation"} Freed-Witten anomaly cancellation
            or the discussion in (
            %a{:href => "#Moore"}> Moore
            ).
