          %h2#References References
          %p The name goes back to:
          %ul
            %li#KalbRamond
              M. Kalb,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Ramond"} Pierre Ramond
              = succeed "," do
                %em Classical direct interstring action
              %strong 9
              (1974) 2273-2284 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.9.2273"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.9.2273
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The interpretation as a 4d
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axion"} axion
          %ul
            %li#SvrcekWitten06
              Peter Svrcek,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Axions In String Theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0605206"} arXiv:hep-th/0605206
          %p Phenomenology:
          %ul
            %li
              P. C. Malta, J. P. S. Melo, C. A. D. Zarro:
              %em Experimental signatures of Kalb-Ramond-like particles
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09836"}> arXiv:2501.09836
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The interpretation of the B-field as a 3-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gaw%C4%99dzki"}> Krzysztof Gawędzki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological Actions in two-dimensional Quantum Field Theories
              = succeed "," do
                %em Nonperturbative quantum field theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 185
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/257658"} spire:257658
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4613-0729-7_5"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4613-0729-7_5
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Gawedzki-TopologicalActions.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p picked up in
          %ul
            %li#FreedWitten99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Anomalies in String Theory with D-Branes
              %strong 3
              4 (1999) 819-852 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9907189"}> arXiv:hep-th/9907189
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/504509"} InSpire:504509
          %p
            The equivalent formulation in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+bundle+gerbes"} connections on bundle gerbes
            originates with
          %ul
            %li{:id => "GawędzkiReis02"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gaw%C4%99dzki"}> Krzysztof Gawędzki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nuno+Reis"} Nuno Reis
                = succeed "," do
                  %em WZW branes and gerbes
                %strong 14
                (2002) 1281-1334 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0205233"}> arXiv:hep-th/0205233
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X02001557"} doi:10.1142/S0129055X02001557
            %li#CareyJohnsonMurray02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Carey"}> Alan Carey
                , Stuart Johnson,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Murray"} Michael Murray
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Holonomy on D-Branes
                %strong 52
                2 (2004) 186-216 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0204199"}> arXiv:hep-th/0204199
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geomphys.2004.02.008"} doi:10.1016/j.geomphys.2004.02.008
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#BonoraRuffinoSavelli08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loriano+Bonora"}> Loriano Bonora
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabio+Ferrari+Ruffino"} Fabio Ferrari Ruffino
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raffaele+Savelli"} Raffaele Savelli
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classifying A-field and B-field configurations in the presence of D-branes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0810.4291"} arXiv:0810.4291
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/2008/12/078"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/2008/12/078
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabio+Ferrari+Ruffino"}> Fabio Ferrari Ruffino
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classifying A-field and B-field configurations in the presence of D-branes - Part II: Stacks of D-branes
                %strong 858
                (2012) 377-404 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1104.2798"}> arXiv:1104.2798
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2012.01.013"} doi:10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2012.01.013
          %p
            A more refined discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            of the Kalb-Ramond field and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-fields"} RR-fields
            that it interacts with:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization+and+generalized+differential+cohomology"} Dirac charge quantization and generalized differential cohomology
              %strong 7
              (2002) 129-194 &amp;lbrack;
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0011220"} arXiv:hep-th/0011220
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/SDG.2002.v7.n1.a6"} doi:10.4310/SDG.2002.v7.n1.a6
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/537392"} spire:537392
          %p
            In fact, in full generality the Kalb-Ramond field on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            background is not a plain bundle gerbe, but a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jandl+gerbe"} Jandl gerbe
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi AUT
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AUT(U(1))
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundles"} principal 2-bundles
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+2-group"} automorphism 2-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AUT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
